window.__CAPM_DATA=(window.__CAPM_DATA||"")+"m could have. If a project has more than one critical path, then all critical paths must have exactly the same length.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The project manager should approve the network diagram and closely monitor all three critical paths. Theoretically, there is no limit on how many critical paths a network diagram could have. If a project has more than one critical path, then all critical paths must have exactly the same length.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":3,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Which technique is used to develop the WBS?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which technique is used to develop the WBS?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Scope decomposition<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Scope decomposition\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Bottom-up estimating<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Bottom-up estimating\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Rolling wave planning<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Rolling wave planning\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Checklist analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Checklist analysis\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Scope decomposition is a planning method used to decompose and subdivide the project and scope deliverables into more manageable, small work units. The decomposition level depends on the complexity and size of the project (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 84).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Scope decomposition is a planning method used to decompose and subdivide the project and scope deliverables into more manageable, small work units. The decomposition level depends on the complexity and size of the project (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 84).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":4,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">During a project status meeting, the project manager updated the sponsor on the project performance, indicating that the SPI is 0.75 and the CPI is 1.05. What does this imply?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During a project status meeting, the project manager updated the sponsor on the project performance, indicating that the SPI is 0.75 and the CPI is 1.05. What does this imply?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project is on schedule but over budget<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The project is on schedule but over budget\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project is behind schedule but within budget<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The project is behind schedule but within budget\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project is within budget and on schedule<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The project is within budget and on schedule\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project is over budget and behind schedule<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The project is over budget and behind schedule\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A Schedule Performance Index (SPI) of less than 1 indicates that the project is behind schedule. A Cost Performance Index (CPI) greater than 1 means that the project is within the predetermined budget.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B A Schedule Performance Index (SPI) of less than 1 indicates that the project is behind schedule. A Cost Performance Index (CPI) greater than 1 means that the project is within the predetermined budget.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":5,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-1\\\">A Business Analyst is assigned to a Mobile App development project. One week prior to the product delivery date, the client requests a change to a specific business requirement. What should the Business Analyst do? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A Business Analyst is assigned to a Mobile App development project. One week prior to the product delivery date, the client requests a change to a specific business requirement. What should the Business Analyst do?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3C-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Proceed with implementing the requested change <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Proceed with implementing the requested change\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Refer the client’s request to the Change Control Board (CCB) for review <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Refer the client’s request to the Change Control Board (CCB) for review\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Measure the impact of the requested change on the delivery date <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Measure the impact of the requested change on the delivery date\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Deliver the product and then work on the requested change<span><\\/span> <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Deliver the product and then work on the requested change\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-1\\\"><span>Correct Answer = B<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-1\\\">Change requests should be reviewed and discussed by the Change Control Board (CCB) to analyze their impact on the project, including its delivery date, and accordingly, get accepted or rejected. The Business Analyst (BA) should not proceed with implementing the change without presenting the request to the CCB and getting their approval first. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Change requests should be reviewed and discussed by the Change Control Board (CCB) to analyze their impact on the project, including its delivery date, and accordingly, get accepted or rejected. The Business Analyst (BA) should not proceed with implementing the change without presenting the request to the CCB and getting their approval first.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":6,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">During a project performance review meeting, a project manager presented the following figures: AC = $4,000, PV = $5,000, and EV = $5,500. What does that indicate about the project?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During a project performance review meeting, a project manager presented the following figures: AC = $4,000, PV = $5,000, and EV = $5,500. What does that indicate about the project?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project is ahead of schedule and under budget since both the SV and CV are positive.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The project is ahead of schedule and under budget since both the SV and CV are positive.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>These figures are not enough to calculate the project’s CPI and SPI.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. These figures are not enough to calculate the project’s CPI and SPI.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project manager has probably spent more than they initially planned to since the CV is negative.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The project manager has probably spent more than they initially planned to since the CV is negative.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project is behind schedule since the SV is negative.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The project is behind schedule since the SV is negative.\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">CV = EV – AC = $5,500 – $4,000 = $1,500. The Cost Variance (CV) is positive, which means that the project is under budget.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">SV = EV – PV = $5,500 – $5,000 = $500. The Schedule Variance (SV) is positive, which means that the project is ahead of schedule.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A CV = EV – AC = $5,500 – $4,000 = $1,500. The Cost Variance (CV) is positive, which means that the project is under budget. SV = EV – PV = $5,500 – $5,000 = $500. The Schedule Variance (SV) is positive, which means that the project is ahead of schedule.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":7,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">The longest path in a network diagram is known as:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The longest path in a network diagram is known as:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Critical Path<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Critical Path\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Critical Chain<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Critical Chain\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Float<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Float\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Free Float<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Free Float\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">In a network diagram, the critical path is the path with the longest series of tasks (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 238)<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The critical chain is also the longest path in the network diagram, but unlike the critical path, it takes into consideration resource availability in addition to technical dependencies.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Activities that are not on the critical path have some float (also called slack) that allows some margin for delay without causing the delay or change of the project end date.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Free float is the amount of time an activity can be delayed without delaying the early start of the immediate subsequent activity.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A In a network diagram, the critical path is the path with the longest series of tasks (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 238) . Option B: The critical chain is also the longest path in the network diagram, but unlike the critical path, it takes into consideration resource availability in addition to technical dependencies. Option C: Activities that are not on the critical path have some float (also called slack) that allows some margin for delay without causing the delay or change of the project end date. Option D: Free float is the amount of time an activity can be delayed without delaying the early start of the immediate subsequent activity.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":8,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A project manager is assigned to a 12-month project that has a $100,000 budget. Six months have passed and $60,000 has been spent. On closer inspection, the project manager finds out that so far, only 40% of the work has been completed. The value of the completed 40% work is referred to as:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is assigned to a 12-month project that has a $100,000 budget. Six months have passed and $60,000 has been spent. On closer inspection, the project manager finds out that so far, only 40% of the work has been completed. The value of the completed 40% work is referred to as:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Planned value<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Planned value\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Earned value<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Earned value\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Actual cost<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Actual cost\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cost variance<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Cost variance\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Earned Value refers to the value of the work accomplished to date (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 239). If the project gets terminated at this point, Earned Value will show you the value that the project has produced. In this case, the project’s Earned Value (EV) is $40,000 = 40% of the value of total work.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The planned value is $50,000 (50% of the budget).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The amount of $60,000 represents the Actual Cost (AC).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The cost variance is -$20,000 (EV - AC).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Earned Value refers to the value of the work accomplished to date (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 239). If the project gets terminated at this point, Earned Value will show you the value that the project has produced. In this case, the project’s Earned Value (EV) is $40,000 = 40% of the value of total work. Option A: The planned value is $50,000 (50% of the budget). Option C: The amount of $60,000 represents the Actual Cost (AC). Option D: The cost variance is -$20,000 (EV - AC).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":9,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Which of the following statements are true about the deliverables of a predictive project? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following statements are true about the deliverables of a predictive project? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project deliverables should be identified throughout the project lifecycle.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Project deliverables should be identified throughout the project lifecycle.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project deliverables can be products, services, or any other type of outcome.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Project deliverables can be products, services, or any other type of outcome.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Once defined, project deliverables should not be changed anymore.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Once defined, project deliverables should not be changed anymore.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The acceptance criteria for deliverables should be outlined in the project agreement.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The acceptance criteria for deliverables should be outlined in the project agreement.\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>The project manager should approve the deliverables in order to close the project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. The project manager should approve the deliverables in order to close the project.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B, D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Project deliverables can be products, services, or any other type of outcome. Acceptance criteria should be described and agreed upon.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> In a predictive approach, project deliverables should be determined, described, and agreed upon as early as possible in the project, to avoid any costly changes later on.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The change is possible and should follow the change request process.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option E:<\\/span> Project deliverables should be approved by the customer, not the project manager, in order to close the project.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B, D Project deliverables can be products, services, or any other type of outcome. Acceptance criteria should be described and agreed upon. Option A: In a predictive approach, project deliverables should be determined, described, and agreed upon as early as possible in the project, to avoid any costly changes later on. Option C: The change is possible and should follow the change request process. Option E: Project deliverables should be approved by the customer, not the project manager, in order to close the project.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":10,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Which of the following statements describes the characteristics of the predictive project management approach? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following statements describes the characteristics of the predictive project management approach? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Scope, time, and cost are established in the early phases of the project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Scope, time, and cost are established in the early phases of the project.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Change is limited as much as possible during project execution.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Change is limited as much as possible during project execution.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The scope is determined early in the project life cycle, but time and cost are frequently adjusted.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The scope is determined early in the project life cycle, but time and cost are frequently adjusted.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>After one iteration, deliverables have enough functionality to be deemed complete<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. After one iteration, deliverables have enough functionality to be deemed complete .\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A, B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Predictive methods focus on thoroughly analyzing and planning the future while taking into account known risks. The scope, time, and cost are all predetermined early in the project life cycle. Predictive teams often establish a Change Control Board (CCB) to ensure that only valuable changes are considered for implementation.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, B Predictive methods focus on thoroughly analyzing and planning the future while taking into account known risks. The scope, time, and cost are all predetermined early in the project life cycle. Predictive teams often establish a Change Control Board (CCB) to ensure that only valuable changes are considered for implementation.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":11,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">In the predictive approach, which of the following terms is used for both schedule and cost to define what you’ll measure against later in the monitoring and controlling phase?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In the predictive approach, which of the following terms is used for both schedule and cost to define what you’ll measure against later in the monitoring and controlling phase?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Variance<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Variance\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Expected value<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Expected value\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Baseline<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Baseline\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Estimates<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Estimates\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Cost and schedule baselines are used to assess performance in the monitoring and controlling phases.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Cost and schedule baselines are used to assess performance in the monitoring and controlling phases.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":12,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sFM-1\\\">The diagram below depicts the decomposition of project deliverables into smaller tasks.<\\/p><div class=\\\"class_sFS-0\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\\\"/><\\/div><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\">This diagram is referred to as:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The diagram below depicts the decomposition of project deliverables into smaller tasks. This diagram is referred to as:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Affinity diagram<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Affinity diagram\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Product breakdown<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Product breakdown\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Product roadmap<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Product roadmap\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Work breakdown structure<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Work breakdown structure\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The WBS is a hierarchical decomposition of the total scope of work to create the required deliverables (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 81). The planned work is included in the lowest level of the WBS components, which are called work packages.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Afﬁnity diagrams classify a large number of ideas into groups for analysis and review.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Product breakdown is a product analysis technique (PMI - Process groups guide, page 288).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The product roadmap demonstrates the anticipated sequence of deliverables throughout the project duration.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D The WBS is a hierarchical decomposition of the total scope of work to create the required deliverables (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 81). The planned work is included in the lowest level of the WBS components, which are called work packages. Option A: Afﬁnity diagrams classify a large number of ideas into groups for analysis and review. Option B: Product breakdown is a product analysis technique (PMI - Process groups guide, page 288). Option C: The product roadmap demonstrates the anticipated sequence of deliverables throughout the project duration.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":13,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The project SPI is 0.8, while the CPI is 1.1. What should be the project manager’s main concern?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The project SPI is 0.8, while the CPI is 1.1. What should be the project manager’s main concern?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Nothing, the project is performing well​<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Nothing, the project is performing well\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cost​<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Cost\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Schedule<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Schedule\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Risk<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Risk\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Since the Schedule Performance Index (SPI) is less than 1.0, then the project is behind schedule. Consequently, the project manager should be concerned about the project schedule.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Since CPI is 1.1, then the project is under budget. Thus, the project is on track cost-wise.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> There is no indication in the question that the project manager should be concerned about risks.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Since the Schedule Performance Index (SPI) is less than 1.0, then the project is behind schedule. Consequently, the project manager should be concerned about the project schedule. Option B: Since CPI is 1.1, then the project is under budget. Thus, the project is on track cost-wise. Option D: There is no indication in the question that the project manager should be concerned about risks.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":14,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">What should the project manager do to prevent scope creep and focus on fulfilling product requirements?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What should the project manager do to prevent scope creep and focus on fulfilling product requirements?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ask the project team to overlook small requirements to focus solely on significant ones<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Ask the project team to overlook small requirements to focus solely on significant ones .\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Make sure that all alterations to the scope are authorized through a formal process.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Make sure that all alterations to the scope are authorized through a formal process.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Prevent stakeholders from directly engaging with the project team.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Prevent stakeholders from directly engaging with the project team.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Scope creep is unavoidable in a predictive project, therefore the project manager should adopt an agile approach instead.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Scope creep is unavoidable in a predictive project, therefore the project manager should adopt an agile approach instead.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The project manager can avoid scope creep by adhering to the agreed-upon change management process. Change management processes have to be set up front and should be very straightforward. Essentially, when a change is suggested, it should be reviewed, approved, or rejected, and then incorporated into the project plan if it’s approved (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 87).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Requirements shouldn’t be skipped, small or big.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Often, it’s not appropriate to prevent the stakeholders from communicating with the project team.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Not all projects are fit for the agile approach, therefore it’s not appropriate to change the project’s development approach just to prevent scope creep.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The project manager can avoid scope creep by adhering to the agreed-upon change management process. Change management processes have to be set up front and should be very straightforward. Essentially, when a change is suggested, it should be reviewed, approved, or rejected, and then incorporated into the project plan if it’s approved (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 87). Option A: Requirements shouldn’t be skipped, small or big. Option C: Often, it’s not appropriate to prevent the stakeholders from communicating with the project team. Option D: Not all projects are fit for the agile approach, therefore it’s not appropriate to change the project’s development approach just to prevent scope creep.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":15,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A project manager is overseeing a project that has recently experienced inconsistent performance and a high defect rate. During a meeting, the sponsor asks where the project is currently standing, requesting an overview of work performance. Which of the following documents should the project manager send to the sponsor?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is overseeing a project that has recently experienced inconsistent performance and a high defect rate. During a meeting, the sponsor asks where the project is currently standing, requesting an overview of work performance. Which of the following documents should the project manager send to the sponsor?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Quality report<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Quality report\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Status report<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Status report\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Risk report<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Risk report\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project management plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Project management plan\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The status report is a work performance report that includes information on the project's progress and status (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 190). The sponsor asked for work performance information to help them gain insight into the project situation and make better decisions. A status report can include information about Earned Value (EV), trend lines and forecasts, reserve burndown charts, defect and risk summaries, etc.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options A &amp; C:<\\/span> Even though the project is at high risk and is encountering quality issues, the sponsor didn’t explicitly request a detailed risk or quality report<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The project management plan is not a reporting document; it’s a planning document that is elaborated in the project planning phase.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The status report is a work performance report that includes information on the project's progress and status (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 190). The sponsor asked for work performance information to help them gain insight into the project situation and make better decisions. A status report can include information about Earned Value (EV), trend lines and forecasts, reserve burndown charts, defect and risk summaries, etc. Options A & C: Even though the project is at high risk and is encountering quality issues, the sponsor didn’t explicitly request a detailed risk or quality report . Option D: The project management plan is not a reporting document; it’s a planning document that is elaborated in the project planning phase.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":16,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">What is Earned Value?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is Earned Value?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The difference between the budgeted cost of the performed work and its actual cost.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The difference between the budgeted cost of the performed work and its actual cost.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The value of the labor used on the project up to the current date.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The value of the labor used on the project up to the current date.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A technique to determine how much of the budget should have been spent based on the work done so far.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. A technique to determine how much of the budget should have been spent based on the work done so far.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The amount of money that has been spent so far on the project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The amount of money that has been spent so far on the project.\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Earned Value (EV) is the method used to measure how much of the allocated budget should have been spent in view of the work realized to date (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 239). This technique allows the project manager to calculate the Cost Variance (CV), which is the difference between the budgeted cost of the performed work (EV) and its actual cost, to eventually find out whether the project is under or over budget. The amount of money that has been spent so far represents the Actual Cost (AC).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Earned Value (EV) is the method used to measure how much of the allocated budget should have been spent in view of the work realized to date (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 239). This technique allows the project manager to calculate the Cost Variance (CV), which is the difference between the budgeted cost of the performed work (EV) and its actual cost, to eventually find out whether the project is under or over budget. The amount of money that has been spent so far represents the Actual Cost (AC).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":17,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>What could be considered as the foundation for identifying current or future issues to support the decision of change requests?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What could be considered as the foundation for identifying current or future issues to support the decision of change requests?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Integrated Change Control<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Integrated Change Control\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Scope baseline<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Scope baseline\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Work performance information<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Work performance information\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Issue log<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Issue log\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C Work Performance Information includes data on project performance (e.g., status of deliverables, schedule, costs), which can help identify current or future issues by comparing actual performance against the baseline.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Integrated Change Control involves reviewing all change requests, approving or rejecting them, and ensuring changes are integrated smoothly. This process focuses on managing change requests rather than identifying current or future issues.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The scope baseline includes the approved project scope statement and work breakdown structure (WBS). It serves as a reference for comparing current performance to planned scope, but it is not specifically used for identifying issues.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The issue log is a record of identified issues and their status; it does not serve as the foundation for predicting or identifying future issues. It is used to track and manage existing issues, rather than to anticipate new ones.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Work Performance Information includes data on project performance (e.g., status of deliverables, schedule, costs), which can help identify current or future issues by comparing actual performance against the baseline. Option A: Integrated Change Control involves reviewing all change requests, approving or rejecting them, and ensuring changes are integrated smoothly. This process focuses on managing change requests rather than identifying current or future issues. Option B: The scope baseline includes the approved project scope statement and work breakdown structure (WBS). It serves as a reference for comparing current performance to planned scope, but it is not specifically used for identifying issues. Option D: The issue log is a record of identified issues and their status; it does not serve as the foundation for predicting or identifying future issues. It is used to track and manage existing issues, rather than to anticipate new ones.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":18,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which tool or technique is used to validate the scope of a project?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which tool or technique is used to validate the scope of a project?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Facilitated workshops<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Facilitated workshops\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Reviews<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Reviews\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Inspection<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Inspection\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Audits<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Audits\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C Inspection is the technique used to validate the scope by measuring, examining, and testing deliverables to ensure they meet the defined criteria.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Facilitated Workshops are used to define project scope, not to validate it.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Reviews can be used to check progress but are not specifically for scope validation.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Audits are typically used to ensure compliance with processes and procedures, they aren’t a scope validation tool.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Inspection is the technique used to validate the scope by measuring, examining, and testing deliverables to ensure they meet the defined criteria. Option A: Facilitated Workshops are used to define project scope, not to validate it. Option B: Reviews can be used to check progress but are not specifically for scope validation. Option D: Audits are typically used to ensure compliance with processes and procedures, they aren’t a scope validation tool.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":19,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Subdividing project deliverables and project work into smaller, more manageable parts is related to:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Subdividing project deliverables and project work into smaller, more manageable parts is related to:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Develop Schedule<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Develop Schedule\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Create WBS<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Create WBS\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Estimate Activity Resource<span><\\/span>s<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Estimate Activity Resource s\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Define Project Scope<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Define Project Scope\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B Create WBS is the process of subdividing project deliverables and project work into smaller, more manageable parts .<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Develop Schedule involves planning the timing of project activities.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Estimate Activity Resources involves estimating the resources needed to complete project activities.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Define Project Scope involves defining what work is required but does not involve breaking it down.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Create WBS is the process of subdividing project deliverables and project work into smaller, more manageable parts . Option A: Develop Schedule involves planning the timing of project activities. Option C: Estimate Activity Resources involves estimating the resources needed to complete project activities. Option D: Define Project Scope involves defining what work is required but does not involve breaking it down.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":20,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A stakeholder expresses a need that is unknown to the project manager. Which stakeholder management process did the project manager likely skip?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A stakeholder expresses a need that is unknown to the project manager. Which stakeholder management process did the project manager likely skip?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Plan Stakeholder Management<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Plan Stakeholder Management\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Identify Stakeholders<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Identify Stakeholders\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Manage Stakeholder Engagement<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Manage Stakeholder Engagement\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Control Stakeholder Engagement<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Control Stakeholder Engagement\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B The project manager likely missed a step in the Identify Stakeholders process, as this process involves determining who the stakeholders are and what their needs might be.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Plan Stakeholder Management involves developing strategies for engaging stakeholders, not identifying them.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Manage Stakeholder Engagement involves communicating and working with stakeholders but assumes they have already been identified.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Control Stakeholder Engagement involves monitoring relationships and stakeholder involvement, not initial identification.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The project manager likely missed a step in the Identify Stakeholders process, as this process involves determining who the stakeholders are and what their needs might be. Option A: Plan Stakeholder Management involves developing strategies for engaging stakeholders, not identifying them. Option C: Manage Stakeholder Engagement involves communicating and working with stakeholders but assumes they have already been identified. Option D: Control Stakeholder Engagement involves monitoring relationships and stakeholder involvement, not initial identification.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":21,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>An activity has an Early Start (ES) on day 5, a Late Start (LS) on day 12, an Early Finish (EF) on day 10, and a Late Finish (LF) on day 17. Which of the following statements are correct regarding this activity? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"An activity has an Early Start (ES) on day 5, a Late Start (LS) on day 12, an Early Finish (EF) on day 10, and a Late Finish (LF) on day 17. Which of the following statements are correct regarding this activity? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>The activity is on the critical path<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"The activity is on the critical path\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>The activity is not on the critical path<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"The activity is not on the critical path\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>The activity has a float<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"The activity has a float\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>The activity has a lag<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"The activity has a lag\"}],\"key\":[\"B\",\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B &amp; C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Since it has a 7-day float, this activity is not on the critical path. The float of this activity can be calculated by subtracting the Early Start (day 5) from the Late Start (day 12) or by subtracting the Early Finish (day 10) from the Late Finish (day 17). Since the float of the activity is greater than zero, then it’s not on the critical path. Remember that critical path activities have zero float.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Lag time is the amount of time whereby a successor activity is required to be delayed with respect to a predecessor activity. However, since the described scenario doesn’t have any information about the successor activity, it does not consist of a lag.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B & C Since it has a 7-day float, this activity is not on the critical path. The float of this activity can be calculated by subtracting the Early Start (day 5) from the Late Start (day 12) or by subtracting the Early Finish (day 10) from the Late Finish (day 17). Since the float of the activity is greater than zero, then it’s not on the critical path. Remember that critical path activities have zero float. Option D: Lag time is the amount of time whereby a successor activity is required to be delayed with respect to a predecessor activity. However, since the described scenario doesn’t have any information about the successor activity, it does not consist of a lag.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":22,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which process is conducted from the start to the finish of the project and is ultimately the responsibility of the project manager?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which process is conducted from the start to the finish of the project and is ultimately the responsibility of the project manager?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Control Quality<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Control Quality\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Control Project Work<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Control Project Work\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Control Scope<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Control Scope\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Control Changes<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Control Changes\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B Control Project Work is conducted from the start to the finish of the project and is the project manager’s responsibility.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Control Quality involves monitoring and recording the results of executing quality activities to assess performance.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Control Scope involves monitoring the project scope and managing changes to the scope baseline.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Control Changes involves monitoring and managing change requests.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Control Project Work is conducted from the start to the finish of the project and is the project manager’s responsibility. Option A: Control Quality involves monitoring and recording the results of executing quality activities to assess performance. Option C: Control Scope involves monitoring the project scope and managing changes to the scope baseline. Option D: Control Changes involves monitoring and managing change requests.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":23,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>During which process does a project manager confirm resource availability and obtain the team necessary to complete project activities?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During which process does a project manager confirm resource availability and obtain the team necessary to complete project activities?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Plan Resource Management<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Plan Resource Management\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Estimate Activity Resources<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Estimate Activity Resources\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Develop Team<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Develop Team\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Acquire Resources<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Acquire Resources\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D Acquire Resources is the process where the project manager confirms resource availability and obtains the team necessary to complete project activities.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Plan Resource Management involves defining how to estimate, acquire, and manage resources.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Estimate Activity Resources involves determining the type and quantities of resources required.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Develop Team focuses on improving team performance, not acquiring resources.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Acquire Resources is the process where the project manager confirms resource availability and obtains the team necessary to complete project activities. Option A: Plan Resource Management involves defining how to estimate, acquire, and manage resources. Option B: Estimate Activity Resources involves determining the type and quantities of resources required. Option C: Develop Team focuses on improving team performance, not acquiring resources.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":24,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>What performance measurement is used to assess the magnitude of variance in a project?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What performance measurement is used to assess the magnitude of variance in a project?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Earned Value analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Earned Value analysis\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Variance analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Variance analysis\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cost Performance Index (CPI)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Cost Performance Index (CPI)\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Schedule Performance Index (SPI)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Schedule Performance Index (SPI)\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B Variance Analysis is used to assess the magnitude of variance in a project by comparing planned and actual performance.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Earned Value is a broader performance measurement technique, but not specific to variance.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The Cost Performance Index (CPI) measures cost efficiency, not variance.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The Schedule Performance Index (SPI) measures schedule efficiency, not variance.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Variance Analysis is used to assess the magnitude of variance in a project by comparing planned and actual performance. Option A: Earned Value is a broader performance measurement technique, but not specific to variance. Option C: The Cost Performance Index (CPI) measures cost efficiency, not variance. Option D: The Schedule Performance Index (SPI) measures schedule efficiency, not variance.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":25,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sFM-1\\\">A project manager calculates the early &amp; late start and finish dates of a new project activity. One of the activities has the following representation. What is this activity's float?<\\/p><div class=\\\"class_sJ8-0\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\\\"/><\\/div>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager calculates the early & late start and finish dates of a new project activity. One of the activities has the following representation. What is this activity's float?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>16<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"16\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>8<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"8\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>12<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"12\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>24<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"24\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Float, Total float, Slack, or activity float represents how long an activity can be delayed without causing a delay in the project completion date. On a critical path, the total float is zero. You can calculate an activity float by subtracting the Early Start date of the activity from its Late Start date: (12 - 4 = 8 days), or by subtracting the Early Finish date of the activity from its Late Finish date (28 - 20 = 8 days).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Float, Total float, Slack, or activity float represents how long an activity can be delayed without causing a delay in the project completion date. On a critical path, the total float is zero. You can calculate an activity float by subtracting the Early Start date of the activity from its Late Start date: (12 - 4 = 8 days), or by subtracting the Early Finish date of the activity from its Late Finish date (28 - 20 = 8 days).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null}]},{\"id\":\"agile\",\"title\":\"Agile Frameworks and Methodologies\",\"kind\":\"Domain Practice\",\"count\":25,\"questions\":[{\"n\":1,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sPA-0\\\">Drag the following terms to their appropriate positions in the Agile triangle of constraints: <span>Cost<\\/span>, <span>Scope<\\/span>, <span>Flexible<\\/span>, <span>Fixed<\\/span><\\/p><div class=\\\"class_sFS-0\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\\\"/><\\/div>\",\"stemText\":\"Drag the following terms to their appropriate positions in the Agile triangle of constraints: Cost , Scope , Flexible , Fixed\",\"choices\":[],\"key\":[],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sBZ-0\\\">Correct Answer:<\\/p><div class=\\\"class_s76-0\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\\\"/><\\/div><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\">Unlike predictive approaches, projects that follow adaptive approaches have a fixed cost and schedule, and flexible scope. A. Fixed, B. Flexible, C. Cost, and D. Scope.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer: Unlike predictive approaches, projects that follow adaptive approaches have a fixed cost and schedule, and flexible scope. A. Fixed, B. Flexible, C. Cost, and D. Scope.\",\"type\":\"mapping\",\"special\":{\"type\":\"mapping\",\"targets\":[[\"A\",\"A\"],[\"B\",\"B\"],[\"C\",\"C\"],[\"D\",\"D\"]],\"options\":[[\"cost\",\"Cost\"],[\"scope\",\"Scope\"],[\"flexible\",\"Flexible\"],[\"fixed\",\"Fixed\"]],\"correct\":{\"A\":\"fixed\",\"B\":\"flexible\",\"C\":\"cost\",\"D\":\"scope\"}},\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":2,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">An organization has decided to adopt the agile approach for its new project. What should they expect to get at the conclusion of the first sprint?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"An organization has decided to adopt the agile approach for its new project. What should they expect to get at the conclusion of the first sprint?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A plan for the subsequent sprint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. A plan for the subsequent sprint\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A potentially releasable product increment<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. A potentially releasable product increment\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A Minimum Viable Product (MVP)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. A Minimum Viable Product (MVP)\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A Work Breakdown Structure (WBS)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. A Work Breakdown Structure (WBS)\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Agile uses iterations, also known as sprints, in each, a potentially shippable increment of the product is produced (Agile Practice Guide, page 101).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The plan for the subsequent sprint is the output of the sprint planning event.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> A Minimum Viable Product (MVP) is a primary version of the product with just the basic functionalities with the purpose of collecting feedback or validating the product idea. It could take several sprints for the product to reach the MVP stage.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> A WBS is a planning technique used in the predictive approach.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Agile uses iterations, also known as sprints, in each, a potentially shippable increment of the product is produced (Agile Practice Guide, page 101). Option A: The plan for the subsequent sprint is the output of the sprint planning event. Option C: A Minimum Viable Product (MVP) is a primary version of the product with just the basic functionalities with the purpose of collecting feedback or validating the product idea. It could take several sprints for the product to reach the MVP stage. Option D: A WBS is a planning technique used in the predictive approach.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":3,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">In projects following the Scrum framework, which of the following questions won’t be asked to team members during daily stand-ups?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In projects following the Scrum framework, which of the following questions won’t be asked to team members during daily stand-ups?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>What have you completed since the last stand-up?<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. What have you completed since the last stand-up?\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>What will you complete until the next stand-up?<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. What will you complete until the next stand-up?\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>What do we need to finish as a team?<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. What do we need to finish as a team?\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Are there any impediments?<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Are there any impediments?\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">In contrast with flow-based Agile which focuses on the team’s throughput, iteration-based Agile focuses on <span><\\/span>accountability through three standard questions:<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\">-<span>         <\\/span>What was completed yesterday?<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\">-<span>         <\\/span>What will be completed today?<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\">-<span>         <\\/span>Are there any blockers or impediments?<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C In contrast with flow-based Agile which focuses on the team’s throughput, iteration-based Agile focuses on accountability through three standard questions: - What was completed yesterday? - What will be completed today? - Are there any blockers or impediments?\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":4,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sPW-1\\\"><span>The product owner<\\/span> and the project team are currently preparing and updating user stories for the next iterations. What activity does this depict?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The product owner and the project team are currently preparing and updating user stories for the next iterations. What activity does this depict?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Backlog refinemen<span><\\/span>t<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Backlog refinemen t\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Schedule management<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Schedule management\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project management<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Project management\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Sprint Review<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Sprint Review\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Backlog refinement involves preparing the next iteration’s stories. In order to make sure the backlog contains the right items for the next iteration, the project manager, along with the team, should review and prioritize backlog items, ensuring that top items are ready to be delivered (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 235). This activity can take place as a formal planned meeting or as a regular ongoing task.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Backlog refinement involves preparing the next iteration’s stories. In order to make sure the backlog contains the right items for the next iteration, the project manager, along with the team, should review and prioritize backlog items, ensuring that top items are ready to be delivered (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 235). This activity can take place as a formal planned meeting or as a regular ongoing task.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":5,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sFM-1\\\">A project manager is facilitating a meeting with his project team and key stakeholders to prioritize all product backlog items based on their business value and risk level. Drag and drop each category of items in the right placement in the product backlog:<\\/p><div class=\\\"class_sFS-0\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,";
